<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Saambou lifts year earnings.</title>
<headline>Saambou lifts year earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    40.0	    vs 30.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    8.0	     vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Net operating income     80.7	    vs 65.6</p>
<p>    Net interest income	298.1	   vs 243.1</p>
<p>    Other operating income   91.5	    vs 83.5</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 69.0	    vs 58.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			54.2	    vs 43.6</p>
<p>    Tax			    5.1	     vs 5.6</p>
<p>Div payable on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Saambou Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company will offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividends, terms of which will be announced on May 29.</p>
<p>Saambou said it expected the positive trend in performance to continue ifto the new year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
